{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA (/rebar-debug) — VERDICT: environment-induced (box-wide disk-pressure), not a reconciler code defect. ESCALATING — no reconciler code landed.\n\n### Failure class\nThe 5 isolated single-hour `bridge_run_failures` correlate with the concurrent **box-wide disk-fill / disk-pressure incident**, not an independent network/Jira transient or a reconciler bug.\n\n### Evidence — temporal correlation (answers AC item 2)\nFrom the ops-sweep ledger `b2dc` (tomophobic-stilllife-mayfly) that filed BOTH tickets:\n- P1 `5a05` (wakeful-ordinary-chicken): `rebar-gerrit-data-disk-high` **in ALARM since 08-26 17:55 PDT, unrecovered**; `/var/gerrit` 94%; **root-disk pressure ~18 flaps, peak 98%, across 08-26..08-28**; likely common cause repo/pack growth ~08-26 15:00.\n- **All 5 bridge failures (08-26 20:00 → 08-28 01:00) fall INSIDE that disk-pressure window** (first failure ~2h after the disk alarm opened at 17:55).\n- The **~18 root-disk flaps oscillating across ~98%** are a precise structural match for \"5 scattered, isolated, self-clearing\" failures: the hourly pass hard-fails on hours a write/commit lands while the disk is momentarily full, and succeeds the next hour when pressure eases.\n\n### Mechanism (origin/main @ b9dd6e3ab058)\nUnder ENOSPC a pass hard-fails (→ OPERATIONAL_FAILURE, exit 1, increments `bridge_run_failures`) at whichever disk write occurs that hour:\n- Reconcile child: any state write (snapshot / prev_snapshot / bindings) or the store git commit of ticket events → `OSError`/`CalledProcessError` → `__main__._reconcile_exception_result` default branch → OPERATIONAL_FAILURE (only `SelectionStaleError`/`AcliAuthError`→INVALID_INVOCATION and `RescheduleError`/lock-lost→RESCHEDULE are special-cased; ENOSPC is not).\n- Delivery child: `rebar._store.push commit-and-push --strict` non-zero (`_bridge_runner.py:286`) — a git object/ref/packfile write on a full disk → delivery FAILURE.\nThe failure is NOT localized to one code path — it is whichever write hit the full disk — itself the signature of an environmental cause, not a code defect.\n\n### Why failing loud is CORRECT here (no clean mechanical reconciler fix exists)\nA pass genuinely cannot durably persist reconcile results or deliver ticket events to a full disk. Reclassifying ENOSPC → RESCHEDULE would **silently mask** a real, data-affecting infra fault and blind `bridge_run_failures` (whose whole job is to surface exactly this). The reconciler behaved correctly by failing loud; remediation belongs in the **disk-fill lane (P1 5a05)**, already owned.\n\n### Alternative considered and rejected: single-project transient-fetch fail-closed\nA reachable reconciler mechanism yields the same signature: in `fetcher._build_snapshot`, this single-project deployment (`bridge_projects_list == {}` → `[_query_project]` fallback → `_isolate_projects=False`) fails CLOSED on a transient base-query transport fault (`if not _isolate_projects: raise`) → OPERATIONAL_FAILURE. Confirmed *reachable*, but could **not be correlated** to the 5 timestamps (no bridge logs in CloudWatch; no on-box journald access here), whereas the disk incident correlates to all 5. Reclassifying that abort to RESCHEDULE would also change \"what counts as a failure\" + touch the CloudWatch alarm (monitoring-design decision, peer/infra lane) and regress sustained-outage detection (2h alarm path → 4h canary). Not mechanical, not evidenced as the actual cause. Rejected.\n\n### Blocker to 100% confirmation\nAC item 1 (\"pull journald for the 5 timestamps\") is **not achievable from this checkout** — the box ships no bridge logs to CloudWatch (only lmn-*/snap-* groups) and this session has no on-box journald access. Conclusion is correlation-based, not log-confirmed.\n\n### Recommendation\n1. Attribute to the disk-fill incident (P1 `5a05` / ledger `b2dc`). **Close this bug as `close_class=env_integration`, `caused_by` the disk incident**, once an operator confirms via on-box journald OR accepts the correlation. Held for operator (no journald access here; env/peer lane).\n2. Remediation = disk-pressure remediation in the infra lane (`5a05`), not reconciler code.\n3. OPTIONAL separate design escalation (do NOT bundle): if ops wants fewer nuisance alarm flaps from isolated transients in general, that is a monitoring-contract change (alarm dampening, or a typed transient-vs-permanent disposition split) touching the CloudWatch alarm — file as its own ticket for the infra/monitoring owner; not a mechanical reconciler fix.\n\n### Scope\nReconciler/bridge core investigation only. No code changed. No MCP/deploy-lane edits. No `--force`. No recheck-to-green."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788064827853158253,"uuid":"2a5f3a2d-5645-4e28-8b59-fe3db3337796"}